SUMMARY:The Pursuit of Truth: The Kosambi Legacy
DESCRIPTION:From Buddhist philosophy and social reform to mathematics and Sanskrit literature\, the Kosambis challenged inherited orthodoxies across disciplines\, geographies\, and public movements. This lecture explores the extraordinary intellectual legacy of Dharmanand and D.D. Kosambi\, father and son\, two restless twentieth-century Indian minds\, drawing on Ram Ramaswamy’s double biography of the pair. \nWhat does it take to bridge knowledge and social responsibility? D.D. Kosambi was a mathematician\, historian\, numismatist\, and Marxist thinker; his father\, Dharmanand Kosambi\, was a Buddhist scholar and social reformer whose life shaped his son’s radical curiosity. Together\, their work shows that ideas do not exist in isolation\, and that rigorous thinking can be a powerful tool for understanding and changing the world. \nIn collaboration with:\n \nVenue: Library\n\n\nTwo Lives\, One Radical Intellectual Inheritance\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeD7vVLvNvF2Sc8g0qLL-ZcFVKSagENJBjMjM00Gcb5jNsMQg/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Ram Ramaswamy\, Dharini Bhaskar\n*Event Categories*: Biography\, Books\, Science
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-pursuit-of-truth-the-kosambi-legacy/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Biography,Books,Science
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail_TPOT.jpg
END:VEVENT
