SUMMARY:Beyond ‘I like It’
DESCRIPTION:What makes an artwork meaningful? This talk journeys across cultures\, time periods\, and artistic mediums to discover how artworks speak in different visual languages\, leaving audiences with simple tools to look at the world around with greater curiosity\, confidence\, and attention. \nThe aim of the session is to cultivate visual literacy; the ability to observe carefully\, recognize that images are constructed rather than neutral\, and appreciate how meaning emerges through the interplay of form\, material\, history\, culture\, and the viewer’s own experience. Across cave paintings\, temple sculpture\, photography\, contemporary installations\, and even the images encountered every day\, the question thus transforms from\, “What does this artwork mean?” to\, “How is meaning being made here?” \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nFrom Looking to Seeing: Art and the Making of Meaning\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n*Speakers*: Pooja Kaul\, Anil Kumar H A\n*Event Categories*: Culture\, Design\, Heritage\, Visual Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/beyond-i-like-it/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Culture,Design,Heritage,Visual Arts
